Subject: [PATCH] wowbox64: TEST BUILD ONLY: Game.exe runs with BOX64_DYNAREC_CALLRET=1 (issue 17)

The engine of main gives the game CALLRET=1 (src/box64.rs, ADR 0027); the engine that v0.3.8
pins does not. For the issue 17 test build only, WowBox64 gives a program named Game.exe
CALLRET=1 when its environment does not set it, and says so in its log. Not for main.
---
diff --git a/wine/wow64/wowbox64.c b/wine/wow64/wowbox64.c
index 8b9d2d3..9eebb51 100644
--- a/wine/wow64/wowbox64.c
+++ b/wine/wow64/wowbox64.c
@@ -507,6 +507,12 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI BTCpuProcessInit(void)
             shortname++;
             dynarec_settings_for(shortname);
             ApplyEnvFileEntry(shortname);
+            /* Test build only (issue 17): the game runs with CALLRET=1, as the engine of main
+             * gives it (src/box64.rs); the engine of this release does not. */
+            if (!_stricmp(shortname, "Game.exe") && !box64env.is_dynarec_callret_overridden) {
+                SET_BOX64ENV(dynarec_callret, 1);
+                printf_log(LOG_NONE, "test build: Game.exe runs with BOX64_DYNAREC_CALLRET=1\n");
+            }
         }
     }
 
